WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.180
It's Tuesday, November 24, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.010
Here's your day in superintelligence, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.550
What a comeback. Days after saying no,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.510
Nvidia just gave Jensen Huang his job back.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.950
The stock jumped 33% at the opening bell.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.830
Meanwhile, Meta's AI chief, Alexandr Wang,

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.620
put it in three words: superintelligence is arriving.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.950
He says what we do over the next year will shape the world we live in.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.120
In China, Z.ai says its new model runs its layers twice,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.510
to match models 3 times bigger.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:53.770
And in Japan,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:58.170
companies are using Anthropic's Claude 10 times as much as a year ago.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.710
Now, the money. Amazon's buying Decart's chip-tuning tech,

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.060
reportedly for $7.5 billion.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.640
Why? Amazon's getting ready to sell its own AI chips, right up against Nvidia.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.450
And CrowdStrike is buying Zscaler for $44 billion,

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.300
the biggest cybersecurity deal on record.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:26.030
Plus, Ant Group led a $100 million bet on Simplexity,

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.590
a Chinese humanoid robot startup.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.020
Over in Britain,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.560
nearly 700,000 women are being invited into the biggest AI breast-screening trial yet.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.520
Mary talks through a brain implant,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.270
and Nvidia's chips will shrink its computer cart to a small box.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.600
The catch? Oregon and Virginia are suing SpaceX over Grok's sexual deepfakes.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.900
And over 150 child-safety groups want AI toys pulled from sale.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.400
In China, robot maker Unitree's shares jumped 20%, the most allowed in a day.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.260
The same day,

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:14.470
Beijing unveiled a plan to bring care robots and exoskeletons into nursing homes.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.490
And Türkiye will now cover half the cost of p

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.040
rojects building humanoid robots for industry.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.790
Nothing's final. Not a firing, not a sell-off,

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.320
and not our say in what comes next.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
